{
  "id": "9a4fa5f5-62a8-4243-85ab-de8edaed21e8",
  "featureId": "cd083ad1-8310-4368-981b-d14c73c20d96",
  "number": 92,
  "shortId": "NL3AC",
  "priority": 13,
  "slug": "gridui-12-fuzzy-search-frecency-ranking-and-per-scope-query-history-one-reusable-seam",
  "title": "gridui-12: Fuzzy search, frecency ranking and per-scope query history — one reusable seam",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Extract the palette's private matcher into a reusable search module, rank results by how the user has actually used them, and remember past queries per scope — with the scope key in place from day one for VS Code-style `>` / `@` / `:` modes.",
  "description": "The command palette should find things the way the user has already used it: rank by past choices, and let past queries be recalled. Requested 2026-08-03. The point of the phase is that **none of this is palette-specific** — the matcher, the ranking and the history are one seam that `Select`, `ContextMenu` and the later `>` / `@` / `:` modes reuse.\n\n## Current state — what exists, and what is missing entirely\n\n**The matcher is private to one widget.** `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/command_palette.rs:145` — `fn fuzzy(query, text, case_sensitive) -> Option<(i32, Vec<usize>)>`, a subsequence match scoring consecutive runs (+5), start-of-word (+8) and tightness. It is a free function in the widget's own file, not `pub`, and it is **the only matcher in the workspace** (`grep -rn fuzzy` finds nothing else). `Select` has no filtering at all; `ContextMenu` has a quick-pick but no search.\n\n**Ranking is the match score alone.** `command_palette.rs:273` — `results()` maps `fuzzy` over `self.commands`, then `out.sort_by_key(|m| Reverse(m.score))`, stable so the caller's order survives ties. Nothing knows what was chosen before. With an empty query every command scores 0 and the list is simply the order the host supplied.\n\n**The host's order is the focused-first rule.** `heca/src/chrome/palette.rs:80` `entries()` builds the rows and `:118` `rows.sort_by_key(|(focused, _)| !*focused)` — the focused component's actions lead, everything else keeps catalog order. Settled in P085; frecency composes with it rather than replacing it.\n\n**A `Command` has no identity.** `command_palette.rs:30` — `struct Command { label, description, icon, chords, on_run }`. The label is not a key: the host prefixes it with the owning component's title (`\"Workspaces › Delete Row\"`, `palette.rs:91`), so it changes with mounting. Frecency needs the action name, which the host has (`PaletteEntry.id`, `palette.rs:43`) and throws away when it builds the widget's `Command` (`palette.rs:200`).\n\n**There is no persistence layer in this project — at all.** `heca-config` only ever *reads*: `heca-config/src/loader.rs:238/246/320` resolve `~/.config/heca/{config,keybindings}.toml`, and the only `fs::write` calls outside tests are `heca/src/app/backend_factory.rs:276` and terminal plumbing. Nothing the user does is remembered across a restart. A search history is the first piece of **runtime state** the app has ever needed to keep, so this phase introduces that file, its location, its schema and its failure behaviour — deliberately, once, rather than as a side effect.\n\n## The keys — verified, not assumed\n\n`[keys.widgets]` (keybindings.default.toml:339) is the cross-widget vocabulary; the names map to `WidgetIntent` in `heca/src/app/registry.rs:266-276`, and the table is consulted only while a modal/overlay is focused. `menu_up = [\"ArrowUp\", \"Ctrl+k\"]` and `menu_down = [\"ArrowDown\", \"Ctrl+j\"]` (:342-343) — so **every key first proposed for history was already list navigation**. Settled instead: **`Ctrl+p` / `Ctrl+n` and `Shift+ArrowUp` / `Shift+ArrowDown`**, both confirmed free:\n- `Ctrl+p`/`Ctrl+n` appear only as `prefix+Ctrl+p`/`prefix+Ctrl+n` (`workspace_prev`/`next`, keybindings.default.toml:115-116) — prefix-gated `WmAction` bindings that cannot reach a modal overlay.\n- `Shift+ArrowUp/Down` is unbound; only `prefix+Shift+ArrowLeft/Right` exists (:42-43).\n- Neither is swallowed by the query field: `Input` returns `Handled::No` for `Char` with ctrl/meta held (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/input.rs:317`) and handles only `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight`/`Home`/`End` (:322-325), so vertical arrows and `Ctrl+<char>` fall through to the host keymap — which is exactly the path `menu_up`/`menu_down` already take.\n\n## ActionRegistry: no — with one exception\n\nThe history keys are **`WidgetIntent`s, not `WmAction`s**. `WidgetIntent` (`heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs:393`) is the widget vocabulary resolved from `[keys.widgets]`; `WmAction`/`ActionRegistry` is the app's action system with `ActionPolicy`, RPC exposure and palette listing. Recalling a previous query is meaningless outside an open search surface, carries no policy, and has nothing to offer RPC — it belongs beside `MenuUp`/`MenuDown`, which is precisely the precedent. The exception is **store management**: a `clear_search_history` verb *is* an app action (it touches persisted state and a user would want it from the palette and from RPC), and if it is built it goes through the full Adding-New-Actions checklist.\n\n## Behaviours to preserve\n\n- Smart-case (`command_palette.rs:275` — case-sensitive only when the query has an uppercase char) and match-highlight indices, which paint the accent-coloured hits.\n- Filtering matches the **label only**, never the description (`command_palette.rs:56`) — a deliberate rule.\n- The focused component's actions lead (`palette.rs:118`).\n- Arity filtering: an action with a required argument is not listed (`palette.rs:138` `offerable`).\n- The palette is rebuilt from scratch on every open (`palette.rs:185`), so the store cannot live in the widget.\n\n## Shape of the work\n\nThree parts, in order: a pure library module with no I/O and no clock; the widget and key wiring; the persisted store in the app. The library half must stay testable without a window and without a filesystem, which is what keeps it reusable.",
