    {
      "id": "1e38ca25-04f1-4466-8efc-23bd8d948c18",
      "phaseId": "9a4fa5f5-62a8-4243-85ab-de8edaed21e8",
      "number": 389,
      "shortId": "FVSZF",
      "priority": 4,
      "shortName": "the-user-chooses-how-case-is-m",
      "title": "The user chooses how case is matched — smart / sensitive / insensitive",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Requested 2026-08-04 while testing T385, fzf-style. **Done in the same session.**\n\n`search::MatchCase { Smart, Sensitive, Insensitive }` with `SearchModel::case(..)`, and `[settings] search_case` in `heca-config` threaded through `AppState.search_case` (re-read on config reload, like `command_palette_size`) into `open_command_palette`. Documented in `config.default.toml` under `command_palette_size`.\n\nThe mode lives beside the matcher rather than on the palette, so any later search surface reads the same preference — the point of the phase. `smart_case()` kept its name and became one arm of `MatchCase::is_sensitive`, so there is still exactly one place the smart-case rule is written.\n\nTests cover all three modes against the same query and text: `smart` finds `Git Push` from `git` but not from `GIT`; `sensitive` finds it only from `Git`; `insensitive` finds it either way.\n\nWorth recording, since it was the user's hypothesis at the time: **case was not the cause of the ordering they were investigating.** A lowercase query is insensitive under smart-case, so it matched every candidate equally. The real causes were the greedy matcher (fixed in T384) and the store not surviving a restart (T386).\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDone and verified in the app 2026-08-04. `search::MatchCase` + `SearchModel::case(..)`; `[settings] search_case` in `heca-config::settings::SearchCase`, carried on `AppState.search_case`, re-read on config reload (heca/src/main.rs, beside `command_palette_size`), applied in `heca/src/chrome/palette.rs::open_command_palette`. Documented in `config.default.toml` under `command_palette_size`. Tests cover all three modes on one query/text pair.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
